{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":2286327,"ns":0,"title":"Distinction without a difference","extract":"A distinction without a difference is an informal fallacy where an author or speaker attempts to describe a distinction between two things where no discernible difference exists.  It is particularly used when a word or phrase has connotations associated with it that one party to an argument prefers to avoid.","description":"Type of logical fallacy","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}